   "text": {
    "L1": "Energy is needed to move, work, grow, heat up, light up, or make sound.",
    "L2": "We cannot see energy itself; we see what it does. Food, the Sun, wind, water, fuel, and electricity are sources of energy.",
    "L3": "The energy in our food first came from the Sun. Plants use sunlight to make their food, and we eat plants or animals that ate plants.",
    "L4": "Wind can move a kite, flowing water can turn a turbine, and fuel can give energy when it burns.",
    "L5": "Electricity can come from coal, falling water, wind, or sunlight. It runs fans, lights, and machines.",
    "L6": "Energy changes from one form to another instead of becoming nothing. In a bulb, electricity changes into light and heat.",
    "L7": "Follow this chain: sunlight helps a wheat plant make food, wheat becomes roti, and roti gives your body energy.",
    "L8": "Your body then uses that energy for work, such as cycling to school."
   },
